=== intro

An automated beacon pulses in the void—standard navigation 
marker, broadcasting route data and hazard warnings.

But there's something else in the signal. Encrypted. Hidden 
in the margins of the broadcast, piggy-backing on legitimate 
traffic.

Someone's using this beacon for more than navigation.

* [Download the hidden data]
  -> download

* [Trace the encryption source]
  -> trace

* [Ignore it]
  ~ chronicle "Data Beacon"
    Found hidden data in a navigation beacon. Decided not to get involved.
  -> END

=== download

The encrypted data transfers to your systems. It takes 
cycles to crack—whoever hid it knew what they were doing.

Inside: coordinates. Dozens of them. Locations across the 
Margin, each tagged with cryptic identifiers. Safe houses? 
Dead drops? Meeting points?

No context. No explanation. Just locations.

* [Keep the data]
  ~ flag beacon_data
  ~ chronicle "Hidden Data"
    Extracted encrypted coordinates from a navigation beacon. Don't know what they mean yet.
  -> END

* [Sell it to a data broker]
  ~ credits += 45
  ~ chronicle "Hidden Data"
    Found encrypted coordinates in a beacon. Sold them. Someone else's mystery now.
  -> END

=== trace

You analyze the encryption, looking for signatures, 
patterns, anything that might identify the source.

The trail leads through multiple relays, carefully 
anonymized. But there's a style to the encryption—a 
signature approach.

Hollow Circuit. This is their work.

* [Download the data]
  ~ flag hollow_beacon
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Beacon"
    Found a Hollow Circuit data cache hidden in a navigation beacon. They're everywhere.
  -> download

* [Leave it alone]
  ~ chronicle "Hollow Beacon"
    Found a Hollow Circuit data cache. Decided I didn't want to know what was in it.
  -> END
